<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<!--
	  This key has to live in a real file rather than an
	  INFOPLIST_KEY_ build setting. Xcode only translates a curated
	  list of INFOPLIST_KEY_* settings into the generated plist, and
	  NSAudioCaptureUsageDescription is not on it — setting it there
	  fails silently, producing an app with no usage description.

	  Without this key AudioHardwareCreateProcessTap still returns
	  noErr, the aggregate device is still created, and AudioDeviceStart
	  still succeeds — but the IOProc is never called even once, and no
	  permission prompt is ever shown. Everything looks healthy and no
	  audio arrives.

	  The remaining keys are still supplied via INFOPLIST_KEY_ settings
	  and merged into this file by GENERATE_INFOPLIST_FILE.
	-->
	<key>NSAudioCaptureUsageDescription</key>
	<string>Isle reads system audio levels to animate the notch waveform. Audio is analysed in memory and never recorded or sent anywhere.</string>

	<!--
	  Required to send Apple Events. Spotify ignores MediaRemote's
	  shuffle/repeat commands, so those two controls are routed to it
	  over AppleScript instead (see MediaRemoteCommands). Without this
	  key the automation request is denied silently on current macOS.
	-->
	<key>NSAppleEventsUsageDescription</key>
	<string>Isle controls shuffle and repeat in Spotify from the notch.</string>
	<!--
	  Required to observe Bluetooth devices. BluetoothBatteryMonitor registers
	  for IOBluetooth connect notifications, which counts as a Bluetooth access
	  request. Without this key TCC does not merely deny it — it aborts the
	  process outright with __TCC_CRASHING_DUE_TO_PRIVACY_VIOLATION__, so the
	  app dies on launch. Note this only bites under a LaunchServices launch;
	  running the binary straight from a shell does not reproduce it.

	  Denial is handled: the registration fails and device batteries are simply
	  switched off (see BluetoothBatteryMonitor).
	-->
	<key>NSBluetoothAlwaysUsageDescription</key>
	<string>Isle shows the battery level of your connected Bluetooth devices in the notch.</string>

	<!--
	  Required to read upcoming calendar events and due reminders for the
	  agenda toasts (see AgendaMonitor). macOS 14 introduced the *FullAccess*
	  keys; without the matching key, requestFullAccessToEvents /
	  requestFullAccessToReminders never prompts and simply reports denied.
	  Isle only asks when the corresponding Setup/Settings switch is on.
	-->
	<key>NSCalendarsFullAccessUsageDescription</key>
	<string>Isle shows a calendar event in the notch shortly before it starts. Events are read on this Mac and never sent anywhere.</string>
	<key>NSRemindersFullAccessUsageDescription</key>
	<string>Isle shows a reminder in the notch when it comes due. Reminders are read on this Mac and never sent anywhere.</string>

</dict>
</plist>
